@startuml j8-ask-for-a-person
!include style.iuml
title J8 Ask for a person (v1.1)
actor Patient
participant "Chat page\n(index.html, chat.js)" as Chat
participant "core.js" as Core
database "localStorage" as LS
participant "Staff page\n(staff/index.html, staff.js, tools.js)" as SP
actor Staff
autonumber

Patient -> Chat : types "Can I speak to a human?" or taps the seventh quick reply "Talk to a person"
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(q, data)
Core -> Core : answerFile(q, data), the file-only engine of 1.0.0.0
note right of Core
v1.1. answer() is a wrapper over answerFile().
The human rule applies only where the clinic file
had no answer, or gave only the phone or languages
line to a message that asks for a person and names
neither a number nor a language.
end note
alt the clinic file answers it ("What is the phone number to call back?")
  Core --> Chat : the reply of the file-only engine, unchanged
  Chat --> Patient : answer from the clinic file
else no answer in the file (or only the phone or languages line) and the message asks for a person
  Core --> Chat : kind "human", status "needs human", T[lang].human
  Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket({... kind "human", status "needs human"})
  Core -> LS : write frontdesk.tickets (one ticket)
  Chat --> Patient : reply "I am not sure I can settle this myself, so I have passed your request to our team,\nand someone will call you back within 2 working hours...", clinic phone and WhatsApp, call-back form
  opt Patient leaves a name and phone (the existing call-back form, J3)
    Patient -> Chat : name (optional) and phone, presses Save
    Chat -> Core : FD.updateTicket(id, {contactName, contactPhone})
    Core -> LS : write frontdesk.tickets
    Chat --> Patient : form replaced by "Thank you, <name>. We will call <phone>."
  end
  LS -> SP : storage event, key frontdesk.tickets (another tab)
  SP -> Core : FD.tickets().sort(FD.byPriority)
  SP --> Staff : the ticket shows under "Needs human" and in "To call back"
  opt Staff look for it with the v1.1 ticket tools
    Staff -> SP : types in the search box (#queue-search) or picks the "Needs human" filter
    SP --> Staff : other rows are hidden, never removed
  end
  Staff -> SP : types in #staff-reply, presses #staff-send
  SP -> Core : FD.replyToTicket(id, text)
  Core -> LS : add {text, at} to staffReplies, status "needs human" becomes "answered", write frontdesk.tickets
  LS -> Chat : storage event, key frontdesk.tickets (another tab)
  Chat --> Patient : .bot-msg marked "From the clinic team"
end
note over Chat, LS : the ids, statuses and replies of 1.0.0.0 are unchanged; the staff reply path is J4
@enduml
